message: "If you use ClimateNetAI in your research, please cite this software."

title: "ClimateNetAI: Reliability-Aware Climate-Adaptive 5G Intelligence"
version: 2.2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23091832"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
type: software
license: MIT

authors:
  - family-names: "Michael"
    given-names: "Olohimai Juliet"

repository-code: "https://github.com/olohi184/-ClimateNetAI-"
url: "https://climatenetai.streamlit.app"

abstract: >
  ClimateNetAI is a climate-aware and reliability-aware machine-learning
  research platform for 5G signal-strength prediction under atmospheric
  variability. Version 2.2 implements the RAC-5G
  (Reliability-Aware Climate-Adaptive 5G) framework, integrating
  climate-aware RSSI prediction, uncertainty quantification, live
  atmospheric-data integration, network telemetry ingestion, rolling
  reliability monitoring, degradation detection, controlled adaptation,
  and post-adaptation recovery verification. The underlying research is
  grounded in empirical 5G and atmospheric field measurements, while
  the v2.2 telemetry workflow has been functionally validated using
  controlled simulated 5G observations.

keywords:
  - machine learning
  - 5G
  - wireless communications
  - RSSI
  - climate-aware AI
  - trustworthy AI
  - reliability-aware machine learning
  - atmospheric variability
  - adaptive systems
  - climate-resilient digital infrastructure
